  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A roof replacement in Utah typically takes 1 to 3 days for a standard residential asphalt shingle roof.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "1 to 3 days"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Typical Timeline by Home Size and Complexity"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "1 Day: Most straightforward, single-story, or average-sized asphalt shingle roofs with a single layer are torn off and replaced in a single day by a full crew.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "2 to 3 Days: Larger homes, multiple stories, steep pitches, complex roof designs (dormers, valleys, or multiple chimneys), or multiple layers of old shingles will push the timeline to 2 or 3 days.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "3 to 5+ Days (or longer for specialty materials): Specialty materials like wood shakes, synthetic slate, or concrete tile take longer\u2014often ranging from 3 to 9 days depending on the material and craftsmanship required.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Factors That Extend the Timeline in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Rotted Decking: Roofers cannot see the condition of the plywood/OSB decking until the old shingles are removed. Replacing damaged or rotted wood adds time (and extra cost).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weather Constraints: Late spring through early fall is the ideal window for roofing in Utah. Asphalt shingles rely on warmth and sun (temperatures consistently above 40\u00b0F, ideally around 70\u00b0F) to activate the Dura-Grip sealant strip. Shingles installed during cold winter months may not fully seal until temperatures rise the following spring .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You can look at detailed cost breakdowns and expectations on the IWC Roofing Utah Pricing Guide _4on0aoepK-KYptQP38C36A4_27 or review local contractor process insights on Bob Harvey Roofing _4on0aoepK-KYptQP38C36A4_28 .",
        "reference_indexes": [
          2,
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is the approximate square footage of your roof?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What type of material do you currently have (asphalt, tile, metal)?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you a more tailored time and process estimate."
      }
